From: Kostiantyn Andriiuk <konstantin@andriyuk.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:48:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: count depth/stencil MSAA samples once

Resource layout.cpp already includes the sample count. Multiplying it by
framebuffer samples again overestimates depth and separate-stencil storage.
On Adreno 506, the resulting minimum GMEM tile can be impossible to fit,
leaving the tile-size calculation spinning during GPU rasterization or WebGL.

Use the resource's existing sample-inclusive size for both assignments.

The change extends Mesa's MIT-licensed Freedreno driver.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
@@ -462,9 +462,10 @@
 
    if (has_zs || assume_zs) {
       struct fd_resource *rsc = fd_resource(pfb->zsbuf.texture);
-      key->zsbuf_cpp[0] = rsc->layout.cpp * pfb->samples;
+      /* Resource layout.cpp already includes the MSAA sample count. */
+      key->zsbuf_cpp[0] = rsc->layout.cpp;
       if (rsc->stencil)
-         key->zsbuf_cpp[1] = rsc->stencil->layout.cpp * pfb->samples;
+         key->zsbuf_cpp[1] = rsc->stencil->layout.cpp;
 
       /* If we clear z or s but not both, and we are using z24s8 (ie.
        * !separate_stencil) then we need to restore the other, even if
